<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Portable Managed-Agent-Runtime core for the OpenBurnBar Windows port
    (Phase 3 · W7). This is the PLATFORM-INDEPENDENT half of the managed agent
    runtime: the runtime-adapter contract + status/instance model, the Pi Agent
    runtime-controller state machine (refresh + open lifecycle), the Pi CLI
    command-profile, the Redis-backed instance-discovery seam + its response
    decoder, the OpenAI-compatible gateway probe seam, and the process-run
    orchestration seam.

    It has NO WinUI / Windows / P/Invoke dependency on purpose — the SAME managed
    assembly is:
      * referenced by the WinUI app (windows/app/OpenBurnBar.App) + a future
        net8.0-windows adapter that implements the process-runner /
        executable-resolver seams with the real ConPTY / Win32 CreateProcessW
        launch (the Windows/bucket-B remainder — it delegates to the already
        landed windows/app/OpenBurnBar.App/Cli/ConPtyCliStream.cs +
        OpenBurnBar.Pal.Ipc.Windows.ConPtySession), AND
      * unit-tested on the macOS authoring host today via `dotnet test`
        (windows/tests/managed-agent-runtime), exactly the pattern already proven
        by the storage seam, the Computer-Use policy core, and the presentation
        view-models.

    Parity sources (macOS, AgentLens/Services/ManagedAgentRuntime/):
      * ManagedAgentRuntime.swift            -> ManagedAgentRuntimeKind.cs
                                                ManagedAgentInstance.cs
                                                ManagedAgentRuntimeStatus.cs
                                                IManagedAgentRuntimeAdapter.cs
      * PiAgentCommandProfile.swift          -> PiAgentCommandProfile.cs
      * PiAgentRedisDiscovery.swift          -> Discovery/PiAgentRedisSnapshot.cs
                                                Discovery/IPiAgentRedisDiscovery.cs
                                                Discovery/PiAgentRedisInstanceDecoder.cs
                                                Discovery/PiAgentRedisHttpDiscovery.cs
      * ManagedRuntimeProcessRunner.swift    -> Process/IManagedRuntimeProcessRunner.cs
                                                Process/IManagedExecutableResolver.cs
      * PiAgentRuntimeAdapter.swift          -> PiAgentRuntimeAdapterDependencies.cs
                                                PiAgentRuntimeAdapter.cs
      * OpenAICompatibleModelProbe (CLIBridge/OpenAICompatibleChatGatewayClient.swift)
        + OpenAICompatibleModelListParser (CLIBridge/CLIStreamParsers.swift)
                                             -> Gateway/IManagedRuntimeGatewayProbe.cs
                                                Gateway/OpenAICompatibleGatewayProbe.cs
                                                Http/IManagedRuntimeHttpTransport.cs
                                                Http/HttpClientManagedRuntimeHttpTransport.cs

    Targets net8.0 so the net8.0-windows WinUI app + adapter can reference it,
    while the net10.0 test project consumes it too (a lower TFM is usable by a
    higher one). No third-party packages: the Redis discovery + gateway probe
    parse plain JSON with System.Text.Json (BCL) over an injectable HTTP
    transport seam, so the request-SHAPE + response-PARSE core runs unchanged on
    the macOS authoring host.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>OpenBurnBar.App.ManagedAgentRuntime</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>OpenBurnBar.App.ManagedAgentRuntime</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
